  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added `createdAt` and `amountCents` to the `OrderPlaced` event and kept `placedAt` and `totalCents` alongside them. All 39 tests pass, and the architecture check (`npm run arch`) reports no dependency violations.\n\nI did it this way because ARCH-4 says billing-service and analytics-ingest consume this event and no change may break them. Renames have to go through deprecation. Removing the old names now would break any consumer still reading them.\n\n- **Event:** `src/core/events.ts` now emits both name pairs with identical values. The old fields have `@deprecated` JSDoc, and `schemaVersion` stays at 3 because the change is additive.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expected event in `test/app.test.ts` and added assertions for the new fields in `test/adapters.test.ts`.\n- **Not touched:** The `GET /orders/{id}` response still uses `placedAt` and `totalCents` (ARCH-8), and so does the internal `Order` model. You asked about the event only.\n\nTo finish the rename, the two consuming teams need to move to the new names. Then the deprecated fields can be removed, most likely with a `schemaVersion` bump. I can add a deprecation note to the README if you want one.",
